From 25baa72adec4ddc294c4f7cd6d11054dbc803897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:37:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(memory): drop stale Supermemory session ingest and gui
 platform value

- The provider comparison table (EN and zh-Hans) still credited
  Supermemory with "session graph ingest", and the SUPERMEMORY_API_KEY row
  (EN and zh-Hans) with "session ingest". The plugin
  (plugins/memory/supermemory/__init__.py) writes each completed turn in
  sync_turn and only retries failed writes at on_session_end; the
  session-end /v4/conversations ingest is gone and the provider section
  above already says "per-turn conversation capture" (bc1d4776db purged
  the other references but missed these rows).
- memory-provider-plugin.md listed `gui` as an example `platform` value.
  No session reports `gui`: the TUI gateway resolves `desktop` (Desktop
  chat panel) or `tui` (tui_gateway/server.py _resolve_session_platform),
  ACP passes `acp`, and _memory_provider_init_kwargs forwards that value
  unchanged.

Docs only; no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
